The second stop, interestingly,

1126
00:55:06,218 --> 00:55:07,470
he commits murder.

1127
00:55:08,440 --> 00:55:10,660
He commits murder, which seems absurd.

1128
00:55:11,140 --> 00:55:13,340
Seems unjust, and actually even

1129
00:55:13,340 --> 00:55:15,850
what Zul Qarnain does in the second stop seems unjust. Why?

1130
00:55:15,860 --> 00:55:18,060
He saw people that have no shade and what did he do?

1131
00:55:19,240 --> 00:55:20,260
He just let them be.

1132
00:55:21,240 --> 00:55:24,320
He has the power to build massive walls. He could have built something.

1133
00:55:24,320 --> 00:55:27,060
But there are sometimes there's a situation, there's nothing you can do about it.

1134
00:55:27,840 --> 00:55:29,910
In the case of Zul Qarnain, there's divine intervention,

1135
00:55:29,910 --> 00:55:32,570
something terrible has happened. There's nothing you can do about that.

1136
00:55:32,580 --> 00:55:34,330
And there's sometimes a situation in front of you,

1137
00:55:34,330 --> 00:55:36,290
even though you might have power in other ways.

1138
00:55:36,300 --> 00:55:38,850
You don't have the power to change it, and you have to learn to let go.

1139
00:55:39,640 --> 00:55:42,250
That's part of your trial too. When do you accept that you don't have control?

1140
00:55:42,940 --> 00:55:45,365
كَذَلِكَ وَقَدْ أَحَطْنَا بِمَا لَدَيْهِ خُبْرًا

1141
00:55:45,390 --> 00:55:50,140
He left him alone and We know more about them. I'm not gonna tell you why he left them.

1142
00:55:50,140 --> 00:55:53,050
Just know that he couldn't handle it. He had to go elsewhere.

1143
00:55:54,140 --> 00:55:58,080
The third stop on both cases in both stories is a wall and a wall.

1144
00:55:59,640 --> 00:56:01,460
Musa 'alaihissalam helped build a wall. For who?

1145
00:56:02,530 --> 00:56:03,440
Couple of orphans.

1146
00:56:04,330 --> 00:56:08,505
Zul Qarnain builds a wall to
help the people because Ya'juj and Ma'juj

1147
00:56:08,530 --> 00:56:09,660
keep coming and attacking.

1148
00:56:10,130 --> 00:56:13,250
One wall is designed to fall apart

1149
00:56:13,930 --> 00:56:15,040
as a mercy from Allah.

1150
00:56:16,330 --> 00:56:18,960
Because eventually, what will they do? The youth?

1151
00:56:19,530 --> 00:56:22,650
When they get old enough, they'll open the wall and they'll take the treasure out.

1152
00:56:23,230 --> 00:56:27,985
The other wall is designed- reinforcement, copper, iron. What's the point?

1153
00:56:28,010 --> 00:56:30,418
فَمَا اسْطَاعُوا أَن يَظْهَرُوهُ وَمَا اسْتَطَاعُوا لَهُ نَقْبًا

1154
00:56:30,480 --> 00:56:34,450
It's by design made so that it never, ever, ever falls.

1155
00:56:34,450 --> 00:56:38,100
And even though it's designed to never, ever, ever, fall Zul Qrnain says:

1156
00:56:38,125 --> 00:56:39,250
Yeah, this is not forever.

1157
00:56:40,030 --> 00:56:44,025
فَإِذَا جَاءَ وَعْدُ رَبِّي جَعَلَهُ دَكَّاء وَكَانَ وَعْدُ رَبِّي حَقًّا

1158
00:56:44,050 --> 00:56:44,950
It's gonna fall.

1159
00:56:45,730 --> 00:56:48,670
When the first wall falls, it'll be an apparent good.

1160
00:56:49,830 --> 00:56:52,460
And when then second wall falls, it'll be an apparent what?

1161
00:56:52,930 --> 00:56:53,550
Bad.

1162
00:56:54,330 --> 00:56:57,240
Both have built a wall, but opposite things are going to happen.

1163
00:56:57,830 --> 00:56:58,250
Okay?

1164
00:56:58,830 --> 00:57:02,040
And yet both of their falling is part of the plan of Allah.

1165
00:57:03,430 --> 00:57:04,840
وَعْدُ رَبِّي
وَعْدُ رَبِّي

1166
00:57:05,830 --> 00:57:09,460
When Khidr describes why he built the wall? You know what he said?

1167
00:57:10,830 --> 00:57:14,660
He said
فَأَرَادَ رَبُّكَ أَنْ يَبْلُغَا أَشُدَّهُمَا

1168
00:57:15,530 --> 00:57:18,640
Your master intended that they should both reach mature age

1169
00:57:19,010 --> 00:57:22,340
وَيَسْتَخْرِجَا كَنزَهُمَا
They should take out the treasure that belongs to them.

1170
00:57:23,030 --> 00:57:24,550
رَحْمَةً مِّن رَّبِّكَ

1171
00:57:25,930 --> 00:57:29,540
All of that is there for what? As a mercy from your Master.

1172
00:57:29,680 --> 00:57:33,279
When Zul Qarnain finishes building his wall, what does he say?

1173
00:57:33,304 --> 00:57:35,570
هَذَا رَحْمَةٌ مِّن رَّبِّ

1174
00:57:36,647 --> 00:57:38,340
فَإِذَا جَاءَ وَعْدُ
This is a mercy.

1175
00:57:39,030 --> 00:57:42,500
In one case, the time when the wall will break will be Rahma.

1176
00:57:42,510 --> 00:57:45,660
And the other case, as long as the wall is standing, is a Rahma.

1177
00:57:47,330 --> 00:57:48,550
But none of these are permanent

1178
00:57:48,550 --> 00:57:52,449
because this life isn't permanent
وَإِنَّا لَجَاعِلُونَ مَا عَلَيْهَا صَعِيدًا جُرُزًا

1179
00:57:52,520 --> 00:57:56,660
Good is not forever, bad is not forever. Both are highlighted.

1180
00:57:56,670 --> 00:57:58,430
It's a remarkable picture,

1181
00:57:58,430 --> 00:58:02,660
one item at a time of all the scenarios that you and I will experience in this life.

1182
00:58:03,030 --> 00:58:06,280
Of Allah's intervention, of good situations and of bad situations.

1183
00:58:06,290 --> 00:58:09,500
And that's a structural overview of Surat al-Kahf.

1184
00:58:09,510 --> 00:58:10,460
Okay, so I've

1185
00:58:10,830 --> 00:58:12,540
fried your brains enough for one day, I think.

1186
00:58:13,030 --> 00:58:16,530
Inshallahu Ta'ala. Even if I told you more, you wouldn't

1187
00:58:16,540 --> 00:58:17,740
you wouldn't know what to do with it.

1188
00:58:18,230 --> 00:58:20,505
Because your minds are somewhere else now. So Inshallah Ta'ala

1189
00:58:20,530 --> 00:58:23,370
I'll conclude with that, and we will pick up our study tomorrow.

1190
00:58:23,370 --> 00:58:25,890
Maybe we'll do one more linear study and then go

1191
00:58:25,890 --> 00:58:28,130
to anchors and then go to the structural study of Surahs.

1192
00:58:29,900 --> 00:58:32,007
اَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُم وَرَحْمَةُ اللهِ وَ بَرَكَاتُهُ

